@startuml proposal-requirement-issue-states
' cumin works - PROPOSAL, not the rule of today: states of a requirement issue, as they could be.
' Differences from today are marked NEW. See the draft pull request for the reasons.
' Every activity, guard, and effect names who acts: cumin, the Planner, or the Owner.
' Render: run scripts/render-diagrams.sh at the root of the repository.

hide empty description

state "Draft (no status label)" as Draft
Draft : do / the Owner writes the requirement

state "ready" as Ready
Ready : do / cumin waits for a free slot

state "planning" as Planning
Planning : do / the Planner splits the requirement

state "awaiting-plan-review  (NEW name)" as PlanReview
PlanReview : do / the Owner reviews the plan and the sub-issues

state "implementing" as Implementing
Implementing : do / the agents work on the sub-issues

state "accepting  (NEW state)" as Accepting
Accepting : do / the Planner checks the merged work

state "awaiting-acceptance  (NEW name)" as Acceptance
Acceptance : do / the Owner decides the acceptance

state "awaiting-owner-decision" as Decision
Decision : do / the Owner answers

[*] --> Draft
Draft --> Ready : the Owner adds ready
Draft --> Implementing : the Owner adds ready to a sub-issue\n/ cumin changes the label
Ready --> Planning : [the Owner added ready, the blockers are closed,\ncumin has a free slot, a sub-issue is open or none exists]\n/ cumin requests the split from the Planner
Ready --> Accepting : [the same, and every sub-issue is closed]\n/ cumin requests the acceptance check\nfrom the Planner  (NEW)
Planning --> PlanReview : [no Planner runs, cumin verified the split]\n/ cumin notifies the Owner
Planning --> Planning : [no Planner runs, the Planner left no result\non GitHub, first time]\n/ cumin requests the split again  (NEW)
Planning --> Decision : [no Planner runs, and: cumin could not verify\nthe split, or the Planner asked a question]\n/ cumin notifies the Owner
PlanReview --> Implementing : the Owner adds ready to a sub-issue\n/ cumin changes the label
Implementing --> Accepting : [every sub-issue is closed, cumin wrote the\nfollow-up notes, cumin has a free slot]\n/ cumin requests the acceptance check\nfrom the Planner
Implementing --> PlanReview : [only sub-issues without a status label remain]\n/ cumin notifies the Owner
Accepting --> Acceptance : [the Planner wrote the acceptance check]\n/ cumin notifies the Owner
Accepting --> Accepting : [no Planner runs, the Planner wrote no\nacceptance check, first time]\n/ cumin requests the acceptance check again  (NEW)
Accepting --> Decision : [the Planner asked a question]\n/ cumin notifies the Owner
Acceptance --> Implementing : the Owner adds ready to a sub-issue\n/ cumin changes the label
Acceptance --> [*] : the Owner closes the issue
Decision --> Ready : the Owner adds ready

legend right
  PROPOSAL. A box is a state: a label on GitHub (written without "cumin/status/").
  "do /" says who works in the state. An arrow is: trigger [guard] / effect, each with its actor.
  Every guard reads only facts on GitHub and "no agent runs for this issue".
  No arrow needs the event "the run ended": a restart of cumin loses nothing.
endlegend

@enduml
